# Features

A feature is an optional layer: a distinct capability inside an epic,
two to four sprints long. Use one when an epic is too large to break
straight into stories. This team's Product Owner owns it.

## Documents here

- Name: `ftNNN-short-name.md`, numbered in order and never reused.
- Format: an SRD in the pinned parent release's Markdown format, with the fields docs/constitutions/design.md lists for this level.
- Status: `to_be_agreed` while it is drafted, `agreed` once it passes review, and `retired` when it is replaced. Only agreed documents are planned and rolled up. A retired document keeps its path, because links pin it.
- Parent: an epic, which a feature must have. Stories name a feature as theirs.
- Changes go through an issue and the corpus gate, never a direct edit on main.

## What reads them

- Stories name a feature as their parent; its progress is the story points of its done stories over those of all its agreed stories.

See tpm help backlog for the whole hierarchy.
